// @name: BP — Negative Context
// @tagline: a rewriting rule guarded by absence
// @description: A Bol Processor grammar (2025) from Bernard Bel's corpus checking a "negative context" rule — a rewrite that only fires when certain symbols are ABSENT to its left. A text/structure demo, no sound prototype attached. Derived by BPx inside Kanopi. Ctrl+Enter to derive, Ctrl+. to hush.
// @language: bp3
// @outputs: text
// @level: intermediate
// @tags: grammar, rules
//
// Bol Processor BP3
// Grammar saved as "-gr.checkNegativeContext". Date: 2025-03-15 10:12:04
-se.checkNegativeContext

// Check the BP data file output and read the Trace file

RND
gram#1[1] S --> A A2 A3 A1 A A /times=5/
gram#1[2] /times > 0/ #A1 #A2 #A3 A A --> #A1 #A2 A A #A3 /times-1/

gram#1[3] <0> LEFT #A2 #A1 A --> B B

gram#1[4] <0> S --> A
gram#1[5] <0> #B A --> A #B

// Result: A A A A2 A3 A1
